  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building resilient livelihoods through nature-based solutions in the Tonle Sap Basin and Siem Reap/Phnom Kulen landscape</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the GEF PPG is to develop the project concept into a full project: Building resilient livelihoods through nature-based solutions in the Tonle Sap Basin and Siem Reap/Phnom Kulen landscape. As described in the project concept (PIF/child project concept note), this project aims to build the climate resilience of local communities in the Tonle Sap Basin through an integrated watershed management approach that also conserves the natural and cultural heritage that forms the foundation of the local societies.</narrative>
  </description>
